    "axis": "can the extensivity question be settled symbolically, bypassing the n >= 15 dimension wall?",
    "answer": "Yes. tr_M(free) = t_p^Z t_n^N exactly (Ocneanu multiplicativity over disjoint strand ranges), and on a homogeneous chain tr_M(atom) = t_p . r^(A-1) with r derived in closed form by exact Laurent arithmetic. No matrices at any A.",
    "consequence": "The closed form REFUTES qou-n9qf's headline. Delta_tr(A) = t_p(t_p^(A-1) - r^(A-1)) is asymptotically exponential, not linear: Delta_tr/A runs 0.254 at A=2 to 5.777 at A=40. The four calibration atoms sat in a shallow region, and t_p > 1 > t_n keeps near-symmetric light nuclei there. The measurement stands; the word 'extensive' is withdrawn.",
    "scope": "Sections 2-4 are for a HOMOGENEOUS pure-proton chain. Real atoms mix p and n, so their p-p, p-n and n-n interfaces need a multi-state transfer matrix, which is not derived here. Section 1 does hold for real atoms."
